From: Antigravity <antigravity@holodor>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sm8750: add CPU capacity-dmips-mhz and passive thermal cooling

Add `capacity-dmips-mhz = <1024>` and `#cooling-cells = <2>` to cpu0..cpu7
so arch_topology normalizes CPU capacity across the 3.53 GHz efficiency
cluster (837) and 4.32 GHz Prime cluster (1024), enabling SD_ASYM_CPUCAPACITY
and Energy Model scheduling, and so cpufreq_cooling registers cpufreq-cpu0
and cpufreq-cpu6 cooling devices.

Add 95C passive trip points and cooling-maps to the cluster 0 and cluster 1
CPU thermal zones (matching gpuss0-thermal) so the kernel step_wise governor
passively throttles CPU frequency at 95C instead of letting CPU cores reach
105C+ unthrottled under sustained heavy gaming loads.
